WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.890
Director Joss Whedon blew the doors off the
superhero movie world with The Avengers, but

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.440
his follow-up, Avengers: Age of Ultron, kind
of left...a few things to be desired.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.740
From weird plot points to mysterious helicarriers
that pop up right when you need them, here

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.830
are a few of the dumb things about Avengers:
Age of Ultron everyone just ignored.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.390
​Why is Stark still Iron Man?

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:24.869
Before Age of Ultron, the last time we saw
Tony Stark was in his solo flick Iron Man

00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:25.869
3.

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:30.039
Stark spends most of that film dealing with
post-traumatic stress from the alien invasion

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:31.039
in The Avengers.

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:35.410
He eventually realizes he doesn't need the
armor and walks off into the sunset with Pepper

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.410
Potts.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:37.410
Nice.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:38.410
Great ending.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:39.410
So long, Tony...

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:44.480
So then, why is Tony flying around in a shiny
new suit when Age of Ultron rolls around?

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.019
We never get an answer.

00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:50.000
And Age of Ultron basically ignores all the
character development and growth we saw in

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.489
Iron Man 3.

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:52.489
Why?

00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:56.480
Well, probably so he can go and make the movie's
villain by accident.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:57.480
Speaking of which...

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.940
​Tony Stark is wildly irresponsible

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:06.640
Ultron might get top billing, but seriously:
Tony Stark is the real villain of this movie.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.240
He tinkers with technology and magic he doesn't
understand, and then just sets the whole thing

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:14.270
to run on autopilot — so he can go party.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:19.300
And then he's somehow surprised when an evil
AI is born from the all-powerful Infinity

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.300
Stone.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.359
Even worse, when Captain America calls him
out on his idiocy, he gets all defensive and

00:01:24.359 --> 00:01:25.450
shifts the blame.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:30.159
Sure, his intentions may have been noble,
but building some fail-safes into his insanely

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:32.729
dangerous experiments might have been even
nobler.

00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:37.259
Or at least run some antivirus software or
something, dude.

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:39.140
​Missing in inaction

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.049
The big party scene early in the run time
was one of the best moments in this film,

00:01:43.049 --> 00:01:46.290
serving as a fun reminder that this is a big,
expansive universe.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:50.150
But...where did Falcon and War Machine disappear
to once the action started?

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:54.759
At least War Machine shows up right at the
end, but Falcon is still nowhere to be found.

00:01:54.759 --> 00:01:59.009
Wouldn't having an extra flying guy be useful
during this gigantic battle that threatened

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:00.009
an entire city?

00:02:00.009 --> 00:02:03.170
And it'd be one thing if these characters
hadn't showed up early on.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:04.170
But c'mon!

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.929
They're already in the movie!

00:02:05.929 --> 00:02:09.780
What could Falcon possibly have had to do
that'd be more important than helping save

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.940
the entire freaking world?

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.180
"Too legit.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:17.140
Too legit to quit."

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.080
Oh, well, never mind.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.990
What the helicarrier?

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:28.880
In Captain America: The Winter Soldier, Cap
forces SHIELD's Helicarriers to blow themselves

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:29.880
up.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.850
And then the whole SHIELD organization disbands.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.660
But right when the Avengers need it most,
boom!

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.520
A helicarrier comes out of nowhere to save
the day!

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.620
That's not only really convenient, it also
makes no sense.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:47.820
The helicarrier was eventually explained away
in an episode of Marvel's Agents of SHIELD,

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:52.460
but expecting people to watch a supplemental
video to explain the plot contrivances of

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:56.000
Avengers: Age of Ultron is even dumber than
this random helicarrier.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.070
Couldn't they have found some other way to
get around?

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:02.790
"You know, I have the authority to downgrade
your ass to a Winnebago."

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.740
"I'm aware of that, sir."

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:05.740
Logicbuster

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:10.650
Fans have been clamoring for a straight-up
Iron Man vs. Hulk fight ever since the MCU

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:11.650
became a thing.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:16.210
And Age of Ultron delivered in spades, thanks
to Iron Man's Hulkbuster armor, which is so

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:19.880
powerful it allows Tony to go toe to toe with
the big green guy.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.340
Awesome, right?

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:26.090
But if the Hulkbuster armor is that amazing,
why doesn't he just… use it all the time?

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:31.710
It seems silly to develop something this awesome
and only use it for this one specific fight.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:36.120
Y'know, maybe the crazy-powerful Hulkbuster
Armor could've come in handy when the Avengers

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:40.530
had to battle a certain murderous robot trying
to destroy the world.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.020
Speaking of which...

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:44.010
​Ultron's dumb plan

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:48.520
So Ultron is an infinitely advanced AI with
a bloodlust.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:52.360
He wants to take out the Avengers...and also
all of humanity.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:55.370
Hey, go big or go home, right?

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:59.090
He quickly gets loose inside the internet,
and though we're told he can't access the

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:03.180
nuclear launch codes thanks to Jarvis fighting
him off, there are still a lot of other things

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.480
he could mess with.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.530
How about the electrical grid?

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:07.870
The water supply?

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.400
The fuel supply?

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.400
Traffic lights?

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.060
Air traffic controllers?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:16.440
Why not hijack every piece of tech used by
the Avengers and turn it against them?

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.030
The list goes on.

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:23.070
But instead of causing global panic and making
toasters kill people, Ultron decides to...build

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:28.570
a humanoid super-body, recruit a couple of
freaky super-rave-kids to help him fight,

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:30.750
and then drop a city on the Avengers?

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.230
That seems...needlessly complicated.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:34.230
And stupid.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:35.580
"What's the vibranium for?"

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:40.530
"I'm glad you asked that, because I wanted
to take this time to explain my evil plan."

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.320
Look, Ultron.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.350
You may be, like, a super genius robot guy
or whatever.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:52.950
But when your plan is officially dumber than
the plot of Maximum Overdrive, you messed

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:53.680
up.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.320
"Uggh!"

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.000
"What the hell?!"

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:02.160
Thanks for watching!

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.470
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.660
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

